# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/bin

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# prof files
profiles/
*.prof

.DS_Store
.idea/
.gocache/
.gopath/

# Design canvas exports (large self-unpacking bundles, not source)
MoniGo Dashboard*.html

# Design mockups: a reference to read, not code to ship. The dashboard's own
# copy lives under static/.
mocksup_static/
new_static_mockups/

# tstorage's on-disk data. Tests and the examples create a `monigo/` directory
# wherever they run; four files from one of those runs were committed by
# accident, so every test run rewrote a tracked meta.json and left the working
# tree dirty.
monigo/

# Compiled example programs.
#
# Each example is its own module and `go build ./...` drops a binary named
# after its directory. These have no extension, so none of the patterns above
# match them -- which is how 502 MB of Mach-O arm64 binaries ended up tracked,
# unusable on Linux, Windows or an Intel Mac, and downloaded by everyone who
# clones. Listed explicitly rather than by pattern, because no pattern can
# tell a compiled binary from an extensionless source file.
/example/function-trace-example/function-trace-example-monigo
/example/monigo-example
/example/router-integration/echo-integration/echo-integration-example
/example/router-integration/fiber-integration/fiber-integration-example
/example/router-integration/gin-integration/gin-integration-example
/example/router-integration/gorilla-mux-integration/gorilla-mux-integration-example
/example/router-integration/standard-mux-integration/standard-mux-integration-example
/example/security-examples/api-key/api-key-example
/example/security-examples/basic-auth/basic-auth-example
/example/security-examples/chi/chi-secured-example
/example/security-examples/custom-auth/custom-auth-example
/example/security-examples/echo/echo-secured-example
/example/security-examples/ip-whitelist-example/ip-whitelist-example

# Local agent tooling (skills installed by `npx skills add`, per-developer
# agent config). None of it is part of the library.
#
# This matters more here than in a normal repo: everything at the module root
# ships inside the Go module zip, so anything committed here is downloaded by
# every consumer on every `go get`. A 24 MB README gif is already 96% of that
# zip; agent skills should not be added to it.
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json
